{
  "_about": [
    "Characters in the game: which rig and clips each uses, move speeds, and what they carry.",
    "Paths are relative to assets/models/meshy/ (copied there by tools/meshy/keep.py).",
    "clips: name -> {file, clip (name or index in the file), loop, speed (playback rate), retarget}.",
    "'retarget': true plays a clip made for another skeleton with the same joint names (Meshy's biped rig).",
    "'move_speed' on a looping clip is the ground speed (m/s) it was animated for; the game scales",
    "playback to the real speed so feet don't slide much.",
    "If 'rig' is missing (not rigged yet), 'static' is drawn instead, with simple code-driven motion.",
    "equipment: slot -> item. right_hand/left_hand hold, hip_left hangs at the hip, armor is a set ID.",
    "Items: 'hold': 'along_arm' points a heavy weapon along the forearm (head past the fingers), tilted forward by 'tilt_deg'; otherwise weapons point forward from the fist.",
    "Items: 'two_handed': true pulls the other hand onto the haft (second_grip_from_end) with arm IK.",
    "'skirt': {to, amount, min_height_m} moves leg weights onto the hips so long skirts/robes hang instead of splitting.",
    "'mirror': true on a clip swaps left and right (the library cast raises the right hand; Rites are cast with the left).",
    "'swim': 'procedural' builds swim and tread clips in code (no Meshy swim animation yet). A real 'swim' / 'tread' clip in clips replaces them; then give 'swim_float_m': {clip: water level in rig units above the feet}.",
    "'outfits': NPC outfit kit (WLD-26): models made on a grey mannequin, fitted over this body; each NPC wears its own mix of head / top / bottom pieces, each with the chance in 'outfit_chance' (otherwise its own clothes).",
    "'voices': pool of designed voices (data/voices.json); each NPC is given one.",
    "NPCs are kept busy: pause_s (standing between walks) is under a second for villagers, the farmer and guards.",
    "Unique villagers (WLD-33..38: shepherd, smith_hand, merchant, dairymaid, weaver, seller) are whole dressed models with one voice each; the layered outfit kit (WLD-26) is retired.",
    "'jump': 'procedural' builds a mid-air pose in code (no Meshy jump clip yet); a real 'jump' clip replaces it.",
    "'sheath': equipment slot whose item can be put away on the back (F key for Rowan).",
    "'lines': which set of lines (tools/voice/npc_lines.json role) a character speaks; a spawn group's 'lines' overrides it (travellers, the patrol).",
    "Items: 'hold': 'shield' straps it to the outside of the forearm (face out, point toward the hand); 'off_arm_m' is how far out.",
    "Rowan's back / strafe_left / strafe_right play while he's locked on and moving backward or sideways. Both strafes use the side-step clip mirrored (sword low, off-hand up); strafe_left also plays it backwards ('reverse': true) so it steps the other way.",
    "Rowan wears what his inventory has equipped (dress_from_inventory): an item's 'inventory' names the combat.json / items.json id it shows, 'worn' where a non-shield off-hand item hangs; an armor set's 'pieces' names the inventory piece for each body slot. Gear without a model isn't drawn."
  ],
